{
  "_comment": [
    "Scenario: UC-01 fatigue/drowsiness — long friend drive (M2 behavioral engine).",
    "",
    "M2 design: drowsiness grows at base=0.5/min + monotony=0.3/min = 0.8/min on",
    "normal_road (monotonous segments).  Initial state: drowsiness=0 (none),",
    "fatigue=30 (medium baseline after a short night's sleep).",
    "",
    "Proposal timeline (tick_seconds=60, 60 kph on normal_road → 1 km/tick):",
    "  Ticks 0–23:  drowsiness < 20 (none)  → NO_TRIGGER",
    "  Tick 24:     drowsiness = 20.0 (weak), above_weak=1 (brief) → NO_TRIGGER",
    "  Ticks 25–48: drowsiness in [20,40) (weak), above_weak 2–25  → SOFT_WARNING",
    "  Tick 49:     drowsiness = 40.0 (moderate), above_weak=26 (persistent)",
    "               blend = 2×0.75 + 1×0.2 + 2×0.4 = 2.5",
    "               persistenceLift = (3-1)×0.6 = 1.2  →  damped = 3.7 ≥ 3.0",
    "               nextRestSpotKm = 60 - 50 = 10 km (near) → REST_PROPOSAL fires",
    "",
    "Exactly ONE REST_PROPOSAL across the run.  The run pauses; user accepts rest.",
    "",
    "Note: event_presets.signal_duration_at_trigger is retained (required field) but",
    "      is not used by the M2 tick engine; the signal_duration ordinal is derived",
    "      from drowsinessAboveWeakTicks by build_feature_groups in binning.py."
  ],
